        "note": "Supplies the statement `poisson_conjecture.variants.jacobian_implication` and the definitions it uses: IsPoissonEndomorphism and PoissonConjectureFor from this file, JacobianConjectureProp from FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/JacobianConjecture.lean, poissonBracket from FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Algebra/MvPolynomial/PoissonBracket.lean, and RegularFunction with its Jacobian, comp and id from FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Algebra/MvPolynomial/RegularFunction.lean. Challenge.lean and JacPoisson/Defs.lean copy them verbatim, with their names, and Challenge.lean copies the statement; scripts/check-fc-match.py checks this against Formal Conjectures at that commit. Palomar does not accept escaped name components such as «math.0608009» in theorem names, so Challenge.lean states the theorem in the namespace PoissonConjecture, with Formal Conjectures' leaf name; Solution proves it under both this name and Formal Conjectures' own.",
